t, we find the partial derivatives of $h$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂y}=-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $r$ and $\\theta ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta , \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =-2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these into our chain rule formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂r} & =(2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -(2r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2r({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =2r\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508382 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186509022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508382 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186509028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508382 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186509032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508382 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186509034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508382 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186509048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508382 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508382 #edb/ref 1045 "The Multivariable Chain Rule With Polar Coordinates" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508382 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186509034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508382 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508382 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508382 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8192fdb4-5ea5-58a8-b9e0-07e9449bea2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508415 #edb/ref 1080 "{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508415 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508415 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "12433c4a-668f-57da-9582-b6ee6515dc42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508526 #edb/ref 1080 "{r}^{2